{
  "$defs": {
    "PackDefinitionV1": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "A named, versioned composition of the parts one domain's runs need (BRD-02 R-02.38, R-02.39, R-02.40).\n\nSIX SLOTS, and those six are exactly what defines a run: a prompt set, optionally a corpus, optionally preference pairs, a selector and/or grader configuration, a test set, and a retention set with its floor.\n\nTHIS IS AN ON-DISK FILE, 'pack.json', beside the pack's directory - not a database-only record. ADR-003 puts the pack registry in PostgreSQL while ADR-004 makes the filesystem authoritative for produced artifacts; packs were the ONE artifact with no on-disk manifest, so losing the database lost every unexported pack and `reindex` could not rebuild them. A pack is references, not data - a few kilobytes - so paying one small writer keeps ADR-004 universal instead of carving out an exception every future reader has to remember.\n\n'Pack' was coined in the UI mockup, not in any requirement, and was twice recorded as a cross-repo handoff neither side had agreed to build. Settled 2026-10-12: MIFORGE ASSEMBLES PACKS from miDataworks parts, and pack authoring, the registry and domain onboarding are miForge's.",
      "properties": {
        "created_at": {
          "format": "date-time",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "definition_sha256": {
          "description": "Canonical hash of this document minus this field.",
          "pattern": "^[0-9a-f]{64}$",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "domain": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "description": "NULLABLE BUT REQUIRED. Null is an assertion that the pack is not domain-scoped; an ABSENT key is an omission. The two are different facts and collapsing them is the defect the nullable-domain decision exists to prevent."
        },
        "name": {
          "minLength": 1,
          "pattern": "^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]{0,63}$",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "schema_version": {
          "const": "1",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "slots": {
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "properties": {
            "corpus": {
              "anyOf": [
                {
                  "additionalProperties": false,
                  "description": "One part slot. Holds a REFERENCE, never a copy (R-02.35, R-02.38) - a pack that copied its parts would duplicate miDataworks' data and immediately diverge from it.\n\nExactly one of contract_reference or external must be present; neither is refused, because an unattributed input makes the run unreproducible.",
                  "properties": {
                    "contract_reference": {
                      "anyOf": [
                        {
                          "$ref": "batch-record-v1.json#/$defs/ContractReference"
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "null"
                        }
                      ],
                      "default": null
                    },
                    "external": {
                      "anyOf": [
                        {
                          "$ref": "batch-record-v1.json#/$defs/ExternalProvenance"
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "null"
                        }
                      ],
                      "default": null
                    },
                    "floor": {
                      "anyOf": [
                        {
                          "maximum": 1.0,
                          "minimum": 0.0,
                          "type": "number"
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "null"
                        }
                      ],
                      "default": null,
                      "description": "The retention floor. MIFORGE'S, not miDataworks': they own the set, this project owns what counts as an unacceptable regression on it."
                    }
                  },
                  "required": [
                    "contract_reference",
                    "external"
                  ],
                  "title": "PackSlot",
                  "type": "object"
                },
                {
                  "type": "null"
                }
              ],
              "default": null
            },
            "grader_config": {
              "anyOf": [
                {
